> this does not belong in the minimal viable set of changes [...] should be split into a dedicated PR

@a1denvalu3 @thesimplekid done, and noting it here as the review thread is now resolved and collapsed: NUT-13 type `0x04` is out of this PR as of fe63733, along with the mandatory NUT-06 `pubkey` it needed. NUT-20 keeps its existing BIP32 derivation.

The HMAC derivation is proposed on its own in #495, beside the BIP32 path. cashu-ts and CDK (cashubtc/cdk#2951) both already implement that draft. #494 adds a caution on sharing the XPUB of the BIP32 path.
